From: Craig Shaw <craig@craigshaw.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:36:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Time direct-page ORA in selected native bodies

Validate byte and word ORA with direct-page penalties and wrapping, preserved flags and accumulator high bytes, event recovery, and saved-stack continuations.

Co-authored-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 recompiler/v2/bus_timing.py               |  2 +-
 tests/run_c_tests.sh                      |  1 +
 tests/timing/test_ora_dp_continuations.py | 88 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 90 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/timing/test_ora_dp_continuations.py

diff --git a/recompiler/v2/bus_timing.py b/recompiler/v2/bus_timing.py
index 4328c03..2899b9b 100644
--- a/recompiler/v2/bus_timing.py
+++ b/recompiler/v2/bus_timing.py
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@ def validate_instruction_leaf(block_pairs, cfg):
                 or (insn.mnem in ("LDA", "LDX", "LDY", "STA", "STX", "STY", "STZ",
                                   "CMP", "ADC", "AND", "EOR", "BIT")
                     and insn.mode in data_modes)
-                or (insn.mnem == "ORA" and insn.mode == IMM)
+                or (insn.mnem == "ORA" and insn.mode in (IMM, DP))
                 or (insn.mnem == "ORA" and insn.mode == ABS_Y and insn.m_flag == 0)
                 or (insn.mnem in ("LDA", "SBC") and insn.mode == INDIR_LY
                     and insn.m_flag == 1 and insn.x_flag == 0)
diff --git a/tests/run_c_tests.sh b/tests/run_c_tests.sh
